      en: "Goya is the second-largest city in Corrientes Province, situated in a fertile region on the banks of the Paraná River. The city is world-renowned for hosting the 'Fiesta Nacional del Surubí,' one of the most important sport fishing competitions in the world, which attracts thousands of fishermen every year. Goya's history is linked to its role as a river port and its significant tobacco industry, which was once the engine of its growth. The city has a charming atmosphere with colonial architecture and a strong cultural identity rooted in river life and rural traditions. Its surroundings offer diverse nature tourism opportunities, including boat trips through the intricate network of islands and streams of the Paraná delta, providing a peaceful retreat for nature lovers.",
